{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1557642-deadly-wildfire-legion-army-to-mob-assault","id":1557642,"title":"Deadly Wildfire Legion + Army-to-Mob Assault?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-01-15T00:46:46-08:00","id":1557642,"title":"Deadly Wildfire Legion + Army-to-Mob Assault?","content":"Hey guys, a little unsure about a rules thing vis-a-vis the Aura mechanics.<br /> <br /> So Deadly Wildfire Legion expends your Fire Aura to improve your command-to-attack action by giving them extra damage alongside accuracy. It also says, &quot;The battle group may immediately take its turn for the round to complete the orders on her tick if it hasn't already acted this round, regardless of its place in Initiative order.&quot;<br /> <br /> Army-to-Mob Assault is Water, and <i>when</i> a so-ordered battle group makes the attack (specifying for timing's sake that you use it to modify their attack when they do it, rather than improving the command action itself), you can convert the bonus dice you gave them into successes.<br /> <br /> The Aura keyword says Charms with it &quot;can't be used in the same instant with Charms of other elements, unless those Charms have the Balanced keyword.&quot;<br /> <br /> Under normal circumstances, the battle group's attack would definitively happen later than your order action, so AtMA wouldn't be incompatible with Aura Charms boosting the command action.<br /> <br /> 1) Not sure if &quot;same instant&quot; and &quot;same tick&quot; mean the same thing. Does DWL causing the battle group to follow the order literally immediately after it's given make these events too simultaneous, or is the attack roll still functionally a separate, subsequent instant?<br /> <br /> 2) If they do count as the same instant, then does the &quot;<i>may</i> immediately take its turn&quot; means it's optional, or does it go off mandatorily <i>unless</i> the battle group has already acted that turn, making the Charms only compatible if you delay the order til after the battlegroup acts and have it affect their <i>next</i> turn's action?<br /> <br /> 3) ... Or can you not even do that, and I'm supposed to read that part of DWL's effect as making the whole Charm unusable if the battlegroup has already taken its turn this round? (I've definitely been ruling it wrong up to now if that's the case.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28948-mj6373","name":"MJ6373","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-15T12:49:27-08:00","id":1557656,"title":"","content":"I think the answer lies in their type. Deadly Wildfire Legion is a Supplemental Charm; it is used to enhance another action that exists within the normal limits of how frequently a character can act, in this case a command action.<br /> <br /> Army-to-Mob Assault is a Reflexive Charm; it can be used outside of normal turn order, or with regard to a character having used their action, as its circumstances come up.<br /> <br /> So the first Charm is used on your turn to enhance the command you give to your battle group, at which point your Aura is expended and you are free to use Charms of other elements. You can then use the second Charm reflexively in an instant that has taken place after you gave the command, which will have its effect on the battle group.<br /> <br /> As far as the Aura keyword goes, I'm thinking it's basically a comment of &quot;they can't be included in combos with Charms of other elements&quot;. There are Reflexive Charms that would only make sense to use in the instant you are doing something, in which case using them alongside a Supplemental or Simple Charm would constitute a combo, and hence not work. But one way or another, the action of the battle group enhanced by a command action can only take place after the command, so there's enough separation of time there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}